WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.270
One copy of the play lies open on a desk.

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.830
A quill reaches in and
writes a note in the margin.

3
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.520
Then a fountain pen.

4
00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:10.190
Then a typewriter.

5
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.050
Then a laptop.

6
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.400
Every age adds its note.

7
00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.300
And each note pulls the
same figure into a new pose.

8
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.260
Hero.

9
00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.340
Fool.

10
00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.380
Victim.

11
00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:22.960
Outsider.

12
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.420
So which pose is the real one?

13
00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.410
In this mission, you'll travel from 1693,

14
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.720
when one critic called
the play a "Bloody Farce",

15
00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.560
to readings of today.

16
00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:37.790
You'll meet Bradley's noble hero,
and the critics who fought back.

17
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.850
And you'll try on five newer lenses,
from feminist to post-colonial.

18
00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:46.040
Your mission: decide
whose reading is right.
